From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Screen-space reflections on water

The opaque scene (colour, depth) is copied before translucent objects
draw; transmissive surfaces march their reflection across its depth
and mirror what they hit, the sky only where rays leave the screen. A
ray that passes behind the scene (under a crown, behind a trunk) takes
that geometry's colour instead of the sky map's, which has no forest.
The clear river mirrored only sky: pale at grazing angles.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0030-water-reflections: river colour vs Cycles within 10%; +0.3 ms
- 0038-reflections-blocked-by-scene: river close-up matches Cycles by
  eye
---
